# Build context exclusions.
#
# The first entry is the important one. There is no `COPY . .` in the
# Dockerfile today, so .env does not currently reach the image - but a build
# context that contains the live GEMINI_API_KEY is one careless COPY away from
# baking it into a layer, where it survives even if a later layer deletes it.
# §8 already records that key leaking once, into the logs; it is still
# unrotated. Excluding it here means the accident cannot happen.
.env
*.pem
*.key

# 95MB of dependencies that `npm ci` reinstalls inside the image anyway, plus
# a Linux-incompatible venv built on the host.
chess-frontend/node_modules
chess-frontend/dist
venv
__pycache__
**/__pycache__
*.pyc

# Local state and history that has no business in a shipped image.
data
archive
*.bak
*.bak2
.git
.gitignore

# Documentation for whoever works on the source, not for the runtime.
CLAUDE.md
OBSIDIAN_DESIGN.md
README.md
